/-!
# The six-dimensional M₂₂ shadow action

The current exports prove the centerless-case linear commutation step and the
seven-point chief-factor obstruction for the actual shadow action. The latter
constructs the embedded irreducible A₅ module and its injection into the local
natural SL₂(4) section.

Both complete source case contradictions remain to be assembled: the marked
transvection geometry and trivial two-core, the G.6.4 recognition step, and the
dihedral Sylow/component/dimension-six argument are still required. No outer
exclusion or six-dimensional recognition theorem is asserted here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
proof of Lemma 16.4.7, printed pp.1186–1187 (PDF pp.1203–1204).
-/
